{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic blender light placement programmatic blender light placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md","fileName":"Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic Blender Light Placement","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic blender light placement programmatic blender light placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md","fileName":"Programmatic Blender Light Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic Blender Light Placement","heading":"Programmatic Blender Light Placement","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Programmatic lighting creates lights of a chosen type, places them relative to the modeled scene, and orients directional lights toward a target. Point, spot, area, hemispheric, and sun lights differ in how position and rotation affect illumination in the Blender version discussed by the source.\n\nThe aggregate bounding box of scene meshes provides a useful spatial reference. Lights can be distributed around its extents, while a direction vector from a light to the box center can be converted into the required rotation. This makes lighting respond to generated geometry i